  "question": {
    "text": "One end of a massless rope, which passes over a massless and frictionless pulley $P$ is tied to a hook $C$ while the other end is free. Maximum tension that the rope can bear is $360 \\mathrm{~N}$. With what value of maximum safe acceleration (in $\\mathrm{ms}^{-2}$ ) can a man of $60 \\mathrm{~kg}$ climb on the rope?\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/Y5hWrHy3A-ZgbIJIoHUDA0q1P0NpQ5nuG8Tj2FJy_Bk.original.fullsize.png\"><br>",
    "image": null
  },
